        "q8": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Is virtual staging legal in Georgia?",
            "answer": "Yes — virtual staging is a standard marketing practice. The rule is not to misrepresent the property: the furniture shown isn't in the home, so add furniture and decor only, don't hide defects or change permanent features, and disclose that photos are virtually staged — MLS rules and the NAR Code of Ethics both expect it. Check FMLS or GAMLS rules for exact labeling; every Bella order includes disclosure guidance."
          }
